type: software
title: "trade-study: Multi-Objective Trade-Study Orchestration"
authors:
  - family-names: "Macdonald"
    given-names: "Joshua C."
    email: "jmacdo16@jh.edu"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-3643-6266"
    affiliation: "Johns Hopkins University"
repository-code: "https://github.com/jcm-sci/trade-study"
url: "https://github.com/jcm-sci/trade-study"
abstract: >
  Multi-objective trade-study orchestration: define factors, build parameter
  grids, run hierarchical study phases, and extract Pareto fronts. Provides a
  protocol-driven workflow composing experimental design (full factorial,
  LHS, Sobol, Halton, Morris/Sobol screening), parallel and adaptive
  execution (grid, NSGA-II, successive halving, Hyperband), Pareto analysis,
  Bayesian and score-based stacking, and regime-conditional surrogate
  modeling.
keywords:
